            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am afraid, this is not an issue with 'mini.move', but the result of the fact that `<C-]>` and `<Esc>` keys are treated the same by the terminal emulator and/or Neovim.\n\nYou can see this, for example, by making the following mapping: `vim.keymap.set('n', '<C-[>', '<Cmd>lua print(\"This is Ctrl+[\")<CR>')`. Pressing `<Esc>` will show the `This is Ctrl+[` message.\n\nMy best advice would be to not use `<C-[>` in places where you don't want to simultaneously use `<Esc>`.\n\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.move'.",
